  "comments": "The standard weight of all quarters issued since 1965 is 87½ grains.<br /><br />\r\nFrom 1965 to 1967, these coins were minted in Philadelphia and Denver without a mintmark.<br /><br />\r\nFrom 1977 through 1979, 50,824,000 coins were minted in the United States Bullion Depository, West Point. These coins are identical to the Philadelphia issue. The mintage is a follows:<br />\r\n1977: 7,352,000<br />\r\n1978: 20,800,000<br />\r\n1979: 20,672,000<br /><br />\r\n&quot;Type II&quot; proofs have clearer mint-marks than &quot;Type I&quot;.<br />\r\n1979S types<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6385ceeface4a.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6385ceeface4a.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n1981S types<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6385cf03a1e6e.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6385cf03a1e6e.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a>",
